[settings]
# --- wil50_d2r10 (Nov 23): wil50's next run. experiments/estimates/wil50/wil50.par (the full run's settings,
# rule 9 at the bottom) with four changes. wil50 has had no run since the Nov 10-11 estimate; these bring it to
# what sko42 and sko49 have, plus rule 10 at depth 2. No strong branching: at wil50's root the DNN score's r45
# and production's r21 are the top two at every slope, their children's shortfalls nearly cell for cell, and
# the QPB size score also picks r21 (branching_lab/root, ucheap); at sko42's depth 1 strong branching took rule
# 9's line at 11 of 12 nodes (experiments/sb_depth1). To add it at depth 1: sb.depths = 1:1 (15 firings, about
# 65 CPU h [e]); at the root also dnn.depths = 0:48 and about 8 h of root on one process.
#
# Path check (Nov 24, experiments/tho40b_analysis/path_check, warm_wil50_d2r10.tsv): PASS. From 48,818, the warm
# dive toward wil50.sln with this file kept the path child at every node, 48 nodes to depth 47, where the leaf
# enumerated 48,816 (another optimal permutation). The highest bound on the path is 48,815.9999, from depth 20 on
# within one unit of the optimum. Every node from depth 1 down ran a cut phase (depth 1: 48,244 to 48,429, 387
# short). 3,389 CPU s on the cloud container.
#
# 1. The bound lab's wil50 policy block, arm hoe2 (experiments/bound_lab/wil50_policy): early entry and the
#    hand-over rule refitted for wil50, less patient far from the cutoff than tho40's. 1.35x and 1.09x fewer
#    iterations on two complete subtrees (the same trees node for node), about 1.15-1.2x on the whole [e]. Not
#    wc=1.4 in dnn.beta_sched (sko49's arm): it made both wil50 subtrees worse.
#
# 2. dnn.retry = 1, as sko42, sko49 and tho40c: a pooled first solve that fails (its certified bound more than 1%
#    of the incumbent below the inherited one) is solved again without the pool, then cold. Without it one such
#    node grew a 236,000-node subtree in sko42-261120, and one made the laptop's nug30 run 15,000 nodes.
#
# 3. Rule 10 (every line, the size score on the children's QPB bounds) at depth 2, rule 9 everywhere else:
#    sko42's next-run change (infra/phase1/recipes/sko42_d2r10_sb.par; on five depth-2 subtrees of sko42-261120b,
#    0.51 of rule 9's nodes and 0.70 of its CPU; experiments/branching_lab/ucheap on claude/cool-babbage-ilnogj).
#    Not measured on wil50. wil50's 304 branching depth-2 nodes make its 14,192-node depth-3 frontier, where the
#    cost is (wil50_feasibility/sampling). The blocks keep every other depth on the block wil50.par gives it:
#    the gaps measure from the root's QPB bound, 46,101, so 0.12 is 326 short and depths 3 and 4 have such nodes.
branch.la_exp = 32
#
# 4. cut.zone = 0.012 (586 short), from 0.0075 (366): every depth-1 node runs a phase and hands its pool to its
#    children (the 15 depth-1 nodes were 333-570 short after 300 iterations, wil50_feasibility/sampling; the root
#    has QPB only), and the depth-2 nodes 366-500 short run one too. Below depth 2 every unfathomed node of the
#    measured subtrees already runs a phase at 0.0075 (bound_lab/wil50_policy), so it changes little there, and
#    the hand-over rule keeps far phases short. On sko42 0.010 to 0.025 gave the same trees for 0.65 of the CPU
#    (estimates/sko42/zone_nov19), on sko49 0.010 to 0.018 0.75 (estimates/sko49/tune). Not measured on wil50.
#
# The comments below are wil50.par's.
# experiments/estimates/wil50/wil50.par (Nov 18): wil50's next-run settings, a copy of
# experiments/wil50_feasibility/fullrun/fullrun.par (kept as that run's record) with rule 9 for
# rule 2 in the bottom block (experiments/rule9_bottom). The comments below are fullrun's.
# The full wil50 run (README.md here): the cpcutt arm of
# ../pipeline_ab/run_pair.sh (its 24 QAP_DNN_*/DNN_* exports, Nov 7) as keys,
# then the sampling plan's depth spec, -x 1:4:1:300:1: the DNN bound from
# depth 1 through depth 4 (dnn.ext = 20 levels below a last-level miss), give
# up after 300 iterations when hopeless, children warm-started from the parent.
# dnn.beta = 0.3 and dnn.gu_zone = 0 are pinned: 34e347c (Nov 8) changed those
# defaults and the gated arm and stages A and B ran the old values.
# cut.zone = 0.0075 from Nov 10 (0.005 before; stages A and B ran 0.005): a
# node up to 366 short runs a phase before it branches, so its children inherit
# a pool. 1.110x in DNN CPU on the complete subtree of a 325-short node, no
# fathom lost (review_nov10/README.md, section 3.5). 0.012 here (item 4).
# dnn.cross_first = 5 since Nov 12: one extra certificate at iteration 5 of a
# warm call, 1.016x in DNN CPU on the node-10 subtree (review_nov10, 2.1).
dnn.gamma1 = 1.0
dnn.gamma = 1.0
dnn.ext = 20
dnn.amx = 1
dnn.cheb = 3
dnn.tight_lam = 2
dnn.refresh = 40
dnn.beta = 0.3
dnn.gu_zone = 0
cut.grid = 5:10
cut.side = 1
cut.warmy = 1
cut.rounds = 12
cut.iters = 200
cut.damp1 = 0.3
cut.cp = 100:1000
# cut.cp_sweeps = 3:1 since Nov 13: three Dykstra sweeps per CP-ADMM iteration
# (review_nov10 item 2: node 5's subtree 1.033x in DNN CPU on the matched
# children, one fathom gained, none lost)
cut.cp_sweeps = 3:1
ship.bits = 32
dnn.beta_sched = two,f=1.6667,t=60,w=0.25,wc=0.7
dnn.cross = 2
dnn.cross_first = 5
dnn.lazycert = 1
# dnn.depths = 1:48 since Nov 14 (1:4 before): the DNN bound at every depth with two
# facilities left (m >= 2 in latest/bnb.C). 1:4 with dnn.ext = 20 reached the same nodes
# down to depth 24 (below depth 4 a node got the bound when its parent was a DNN miss)
# and left the depths below 24 to QPB alone, where a run that must find or beat
# the incumbent goes on its way to a leaf (experiments/estimates/README.md).
dnn.maxgap = 1
dnn.giveup = 300
dnn.depths = 3:4
dnn.warm = 1
dnn.warm_y = 2
cut.zone = 1
cut.maxdepth = 3
cut.stall = 0
cut.freeze = 0
cut.cp_iters = 2000
cut.giveup = 100000000:0
cut.giveup_depth = 0
pool.on = 0
